& [UserIntent] is Cantor as an inference co-processor callable from Codex
  + Cantor should be simplifiable to a basic tool without requiring a modified llama.cpp
  + an agent supplies stimulus and receives a hardened attention procedure handle suitable for later inference
  + tools must remain under Honesty and Security identity boundaries

& [ObservedSystem] already has two distinct working surfaces
  + query_sop is a one-tool Rust MCP adapter for deterministic signed SOP queries
  + the isolated EVO-X2 Needle runtime is a learned route selector with exact grounding admission accounts immutable evidence and semantic evidence verification

& [RequiredSeam] is separate experimental learned routing
  + expose one route_attention tool and do not add it to or rename query_sop
  + execute only route-only selection; do not call Cantor semantic query or llama.cpp articulation from this tool
  + require the pinned runtime controller configuration deployment and result identities
  + after a selected route is emitted independently verify its archived evidence and admission account before returning success
  + preserve learned proposal as proposal rather than signed semantic authority
  + reject malformed oversized timed-out drifted partial or unverifiable results with typed visible faults

& [OperationalBoundary] is local STDIO MCP
  + no shell string construction network listener trust-store mutation signing key write operation effect expansion or hidden-state access
  + subprocess arguments are direct and bounded
  + tool is read-only and non-destructive but not represented as semantically idempotent because learned model execution may vary
  + operator registration remains explicit and is not performed by repository code

& [Deferred] includes full inference MCP shared multi-agent negotiation runtime training procedure authoring and production signing
